Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:13:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] vulkan/device-select: only match PCI devices against the
 display's device

device_select_find_wayland_pci_default() and the X11 variant read
businfo.pci/deviceinfo.pci of the device the compositor (linux-dmabuf
main device, wl_drm) or the X server (DRI3) names, without checking the
bus type. For a platform device those unions hold other pointers, so
every Vulkan instance with a Wayland or X11 surface extension crashed in
vkEnumeratePhysicalDevices. That is what happens on WSL, where the
compositor's render node is vgem.

Skip the display-device match when that device is not on the PCI bus.

Generated-by: LLM
---
 src/vulkan/device-select-layer/device_select_wayland.c | 4 +++-
 src/vulkan/device-select-layer/device_select_x11.c     | 5 +++++
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/vulkan/device-select-layer/device_select_wayland.c b/src/vulkan/device-select-layer/device_select_wayland.c
index 29ead33..c91901e 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/device-select-layer/device_select_wayland.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/device-select-layer/device_select_wayland.c
@@ -235,7 +235,9 @@ device_select_find_wayland_pci_default(struct device_pci_info *devices, uint32_t
       target = info.drm_dev_info;
    }
 #endif
-   if (target == NULL) {
+   /* Only PCI devices can be matched. A platform device such as vgem (the render node of a compositor
+    * on WSL) has no pci info: its businfo/deviceinfo unions hold other pointers. */
+   if (target == NULL || target->bustype != DRM_BUS_PCI) {
       goto done;
    }
 
diff --git a/src/vulkan/device-select-layer/device_select_x11.c b/src/vulkan/device-select-layer/device_select_x11.c
index 44313aa..77eb3bd 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/device-select-layer/device_select_x11.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/device-select-layer/device_select_x11.c
@@ -98,6 +98,11 @@ device_select_find_xcb_pci_default(struct device_pci_info *devices, uint32_t dev
    if (ret < 0)
       goto out;
 
+   /* Only PCI devices can be matched. A platform device such as vgem (WSL) has no pci info: its
+    * businfo/deviceinfo unions hold other pointers. */
+   if (xdev->bustype != DRM_BUS_PCI)
+      goto out;
+
    for (unsigned i = 0; i < device_count; i++) {
       if (devices[i].has_bus_info) {
